read those tuples and realize them into meaning or behavior.\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:31:Concretely, a DaoSpace is **a collection of file-backed dao.streams**. `dao.space/open!` returns a **handle** to that collection; the handle plays two roles. As a **factory**, it opens member write logs — `ds/open!` delegates through the space to realize a `dao.stream.file` member, and `ds/append!` appends datom frames to it. As a **read target**, the handle answers questions over *all* member logs at once: `dao.space/q` (Datalog) and `dao.space/match` (datom pattern). The asymmetry is deliberate — **writing is streaming, reading is querying.** You never read the space *as* a stream; member streams carry datoms in, the space answers questions out.\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:50:DaoSpace = a collection of file-backed dao.streams (member logs) whose union of\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:58:any coherent bundle of those tuples — data, a dao.stream descriptor, yin.vm AST,\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:87:appended to one of its member dao.streams. You open a member log through the space\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:88:handle (`(ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space ...})`) and append with that\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:89:stream's own `put!`. Each `ds/open!` returns a **distinct** `dao.stream.file` with\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:93:agent opened once (`ds` aliases `dao.stream`).\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:99:(`dao.stream.file`, opened via `ds/open!`) carry datoms **in**; the space answers\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:107:      log   (ds/open! {:type :dao-stream :space space})] ; my own member write log\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:164:│ dao.stream.file  │  │ dao.stream.file  │  ...  (byte stream: async disk,\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:165:│ (byte substrate) │  │ (byte substrate) │       non-blocking — see dao.stream.file.md)\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:169:Three layers: **`dao.stream.file`** (a non-blocking byte stream over a file) →\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:188: 