e not-found close following the disclaimer frame. Code `4002` is a protocol-error teardown. For an established attachment, completion of a 4002 teardown deposits exactly one `:ws/closed` at both the endpoint that initiated the close and the peer that observed it. The detecting endpoint therefore deposits `:ws/error` first and `:ws/closed` when the connection terminates. Before client resolution, closure before `:ws/accept` or `:ws/disclaim` deposits `:ws/transport-error` and then the single `:ws/closed`; after `:ws/disclaim`, it deposits `:ws/not-found` and then `:ws/closed`. Every other peer close or connection loss maps to `:ws/closed` under the exactly-once lifecycle rule.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:1:# dao.stream.file — Design / Plan\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:9:{:dao.stream/type :file\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:30:Three file transports, three jobs — `dao.stream.file` deliberately does **not**\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:36:- `dao.stream.file` — live-tail bridge: post-open reads see post-open writes, a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:43:dao.stream `next` and `put!` return immediately and never block waiting for I/O.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:76:`src/cljc/dao/stream/` today.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:78:`dao.stream.file` departs from this deliberately: `put!` honors the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:91:### 1. A bounded ringbuffer stream (`dao.stream.ringbuffer`, capacity N, :evict-oldest)\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:102:Defaults: `:capacity 1024`, `:eviction-policy :evict-oldest`. `dao.stream.file`\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:256:1. **`src/cljc/dao/stream/file.cljc`** — a `FileStream` defrecord wrapping a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:263:   Carries `#?(:cljs (:require-macros [dao.stream]))` for cljs `defopen`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:267:2. **`test/dao/stream/file_test.cljc`** (`.cljc`, not `.clj`) — 8 cases,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.file.md:272:   existing `.clj`-only helpers in `test/dao/stream/file_input_strea