`:dao.stream/type` — a qualified keyword naming the transport. This is the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:251:own keys returns `:dao.stream/invalid-spec`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:257:- It carries `:dao.stream/type` — the transport, as above — as its dispatch\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:260:  `:dao.stream/identity` key. Different descriptors may reach\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:267:  `:dao.stream/invalid-descriptor`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:273:  `attach!` success map carries the value under `:dao.stream/attachment`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:291:on a live handle returns `:dao.stream/ok` with `:dao.stream/descriptor`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:293:`:dao.stream/identity`, equal through every handle and descriptor for the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:310:| `:dao.stream/ok`              | A new logical stream exists, its identity settled at once. Implies not that every resource backing it has finished being acquired. | `:dao.stream/handle` |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:311:| `:dao.stream/invalid-spec`    | The creation specification is malformed.      | —                    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:312:| `:dao.stream/not-found`       | No transport here matches `:dao.stream/type`. | —                    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:313:| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The handler failed.                           | —                    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:319:| `:dao.stream/ok`                 | A handle exists through which this attachment is operated. Implies neither that a far end has confirmed the stream it names nor that establishment has completed. Where either answer is one only the far end can give, it arrives later as data, on the channel the transport names (see Surfaces). | `:dao.stream/handle`, and `:dao.stream/attachment` where the transport distinguishes attachments |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:320:| `:dao.stream/invalid-descriptor` | The descriptor is malformed.                                                        | —                    |\