come set is therefore `:dao.stream/ok` (with\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:490:  `:dao.stream/cursor`), `:dao.stream/invalid-anchor`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:491:  `:dao.stream/closed`, and `:dao.stream/transport-error`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:493:  its `:dao.stream/newest` cursor **before** invoking that operation. Minting\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:496:- **A freshly minted `:dao.stream/oldest` is a position, not a claim about\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:505:  history was lost, mints an **origin cursor** — `:dao.stream/oldest` before\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:507:  observe events caused by an operation mints `:dao.stream/newest` before\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:540:| `:dao.stream/ok`              | A value was observed.                                                         | `:dao.stream/value`, `:dao.stream/cursor` (successor)                                   |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:541:| `:dao.stream/blocked`         | Nothing at this position yet; retry later.                                    | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:542:| `:dao.stream/end`             | What this handle is on is closed and this position is past the retained tail. | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:543:| `:dao.stream/gap`             | This position was evicted.                                                    | `:dao.stream/cursor` (earliest retained position, or the tail when nothing is retained) |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:544:| `:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch` | The cursor was minted by a different logical stream.                          | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:545:| `:dao.stream/invalid-cursor`  | The value is not a cursor.                                                    | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:546:| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the read; nothing was observed.               | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:560:| `:dao.stream/ok`              | The value is accepted at the next position in the sequence this handle's writer surface is on. Implies neither local readability nor remote delivery. | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:561:| `:dao.stream/full`            | The transport does not accept the value; nothing was appended. Whether this is transient or permanent is the transport's declared nature (see Retention and Gaps). | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:562:| `:dao.stream/invalid-value`   | The transport cannot carry this value (for example, it cannot be encoded); nothing was appended.                                                     | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:563:| `:dao.stream/closed`          | What this handle is on is closed to new appends; the value was not appended.                                                                         | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:564:| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the append; nothing was appended.                                                                                    | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:581:is also `:dao.stream/ok`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:599:`:dao.stream/closed` and `:dao.stream/end` are handle-relative: they speak of\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:618:- Subsequent `append!` returns `:dao.stream/closed`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:619:- A reader that exhausts retained history receives `:dao.stream/end` instead\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:620:  of `:dao.stream/blocked`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:640:`:dao.stream/blocked` and then a value has not caught the stream in a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:792:`dao.stream` exists to protect a working system while its consumers move,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:794:and legacy `dao.stream` is deleted, **`dao.stream` is renamed to\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:795:`dao.stream`** — decided, not left open. An undecided coexistence of both\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:799:`dao.stream.implementation-plan.md`, was consumed when its phases\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:805:`dao.stream.relation` transport was eliminated with `query`), `dao.jing`'s\ndocs/design/dao.gui.md:21:It does not paint, does not subscribe to `dao.stream` cursors, does not\ndocs/design/dao.gui.md:44:Each arrow is either a direct function call or a `dao.stream` boundary.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:8:- Descriptor: `{:dao.stream/type :udp …}`\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:9:- Handle: `open!` multimethod dispatches on `:dao.stream/type :udp`\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:27:{:dao.stream/type :udp\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:40:- `:dao.stream/type` – must be `:udp`.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:55:{:dao.stream/type :udp\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:75:The `open!` multimethod dispatches on `:dao.stream/type :udp` and returns an instance of `UdpTransport`.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:80:(defmethod dao.stream/open! :udp\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:333:{:dao.stream/type :udp, :host \"...\", :port 9000, :capacity 1000}\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:358:8. **Test with dao.stream.apply** using UDP streams for request‑response.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:368:**Gap policy**: The transport returns `:daostream/gap`. The interpreter decides what to do: skip, wait, or abort. The scheduler’s `check‑wait‑set` will keep the waiter in the wait‑set, retrying `next` each idle cycle. If the gap is permanent, the waiter stays blocked forever; a timeout must be applied at the application layer (e.g., `:dao.stream.apply/call‑timeout`).\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:370:## Integration with dao.stream.apply\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:372:dao.stream.apply uses two streams: `call‑in` (requests) and `call‑out` (responses). Both can be UDP streams.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:378:  {:call-in  {:dao.stream/type :udp\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:381:   :call-out {:dao.stream/type :udp\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:398:Create `src/cljc/dao/stream/udp.cljc` (platform‑agnostic) and `src/clj/dao/stream/udp_jvm.clj` (JVM‑specific socket code). Use `^:conditional` reader tags for multi‑platform support.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:423:Separate namespace `dao.stream.drds` with functions `wrap‑drds` that takes a raw UDP socket and returns a DRDS‑enhanced socket. The DRDS layer manages sequencing, ACKs, retransmission timers (using `java.util.concurrent.ScheduledExecutorService` or JS `setInterval`).\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:427:In `dao.stream` namespace, add `defmethod` for `:udp`.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:460:4. **dao.stream.apply integration**: VM ↔ bridge over UDP, verify request‑response.\ndocs/design/daostream-udp-design.md:476:- [dao.stream.apply Design](./daocall-design.md) – async request‑response over streams.\ndocs/design/telemetry-ui-design.md:18:│   └── dao.stream.apply req/resp           ↓ repl/serve!\ndocs/design/telemetry-ui-design.md:27:- REPL: `dao.stream.apply` uses request/response pairs. Caller must poll for matching response.\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:63: :telemetry-stream nil | <dao.stream>    ; Stream for VM telemetry datoms\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:64: :remote-stream   nil | <dao.stream>}    ; WebSocket connection to remote shell\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:144:Expose the shell as a WebSocket server. Accept remote clients and dispatch `:op/eval`, `:op/vm`, `:op/lang`, `:op/reset` requests via `dao.stream.apply` protocol.\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:334:Remote clients connect and send requests via `dao.stream.apply`:\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:337:{:dao.stream.apply/id   \"req-123\"\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:338: :dao.stream.apply/op   :op/eval\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:339: :dao.stream.apply/args [\"(+ 1 2)\"]}\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:345:{:dao.stream.apply/id    \"req-123\"\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:346: :dao.stream.apply/value \"3\"}\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:353:When telemetry is enabled, the VM emits `[e a v t m]` datom snapshots to a `dao.stream`. Each snapshot captures the full CESK state:\ndocs/design/yin-repl-design.md:459:- **DAO Stream:** `src/cljc/dao/stream.cljc`\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:6:`yin.vm`, `dao.stream`, `dao.db`, `dao.space`, and copied transformer kernels\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:12:there is no first-class operation that injects a new `dao.stream` into the\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:36:- `dao.stream` carries requests, effects, results, tokens, intents, and errors.\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:49:dao.stream request/control events\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:74:- admitting inference requests from `dao.stream`\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:92:- replacing `dao.db`, `dao.space`, `dao.stream`, or `yin.vm`\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:322:- `dao.stream` for append-only event history\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:414:- scan or subscribe to `dao.stream` sources\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:442:- explicit `dao.stream` histories\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:554:- append accepted messages to `dao.stream`\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:695:-> dao.db / dao.space / dao.stream\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:734:These continuations coordinate through `dao.stream` and preserve lineage through\ndocs/design/dao.nao.md:816:- token, completion, batch, and telemetry datoms are appended to `dao.stream`\ndocs/design/yin.vm-portability.md:150:    :dao.stream.apply/call\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
